                <pb facs="0420" n="306" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">875.00/122: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Albania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tirana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-05-18T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 18,
                                1924</hi> [<hi rendition="#italic">—12
                        noon</hi>]</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>43. My telegram number 40 of May 4, noon. …</p>
                <p>Arms are being distributed here to reserves and others. Movement on Scutari
                    planned for this week. A portion of Tirana garrison of doubtful loyalty. Should
                    south join rebels, which seems probable, telegraph lines would be cut. I
                    recommend that a destroyer be sent to Durazzo for communication purposes. Copy
                    to European Information Center.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
